# Line endings are part of this package's contract, not a style preference.
#
# environment/data/corpus/manifest.sha256 pins the byte content of every vendored WFDB
# record. With no rules here, Git's autocrlf rewrote LF to CRLF in the .hea headers on
# checkout, and the manifest silently stopped holding: the headers no longer hashed to
# their recorded digests, and `sha256sum -c` could not parse the manifest at all once its
# own lines had gained a trailing CR. What is committed was always correct -- the damage
# happened in the working tree, which is also what `docker build` copies into the image.
# Marking these paths non-text stops Git transforming them on any platform.
*.hea           -text
*.mat           -text
*.dat           -text
manifest.sha256 -text

# Shell scripts run inside a Linux container. A CRLF shebang there fails with
# "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M" -- a confusing way to lose an hour.
*.sh            text eol=lf

# Read by the Linux Docker daemon, not by an editor on the host.
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
